{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"stars":1},1],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"sections":1},[2,8],{"title":3,"pages":4},"",[5],{"title":6,"slug":7},"Introduction","index",{"title":9,"pages":10},"berm",[11,14,17,20,23,26],{"title":12,"slug":13},"Overview","berm/overview",{"title":15,"slug":16},"Writing a Program","berm/writing-a-program",{"title":18,"slug":19},"The Guest API","berm/guest-api",{"title":21,"slug":22},"The Manifest","berm/manifest",{"title":24,"slug":25},"Publishing a Program","berm/publishing",{"title":27,"slug":28},"Running the Service","berm/service"],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"slug":1,"title":2,"description":3,"toc":4,"html":30,"prev":31,"next":34},"berm/guest-api","The Guest API","What berm-lang gives a program past its arguments: who called, state, a database, logs, HTTP, other programs, wakes, the clock and randomness.",[5,9,12,15,18,21,24,27],{"depth":6,"id":7,"text":8},2,"who-called","Who called",{"depth":6,"id":10,"text":11},"state","State",{"depth":6,"id":13,"text":14},"a-database","A database",{"depth":6,"id":16,"text":17},"logs","Logs",{"depth":6,"id":19,"text":20},"http","HTTP",{"depth":6,"id":22,"text":23},"other-programs","Other programs",{"depth":6,"id":25,"text":26},"wakes","Wakes",{"depth":6,"id":28,"text":29},"the-clock-and-randomness","The clock and randomness","\u003Cp>Each function here is a syscall. berm serves the call's own context — caller,\nuser, \u003Ccode>vouch\u003C/code>, client, the clock, \u003Ccode>trace\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>deny\u003C/code> — and \u003Ccode>berm.call\u003C/code>. The rest are\nserved by the host the program is deployed to, and a call its host does not\nserve traps.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>A program lists the syscalls it makes past berm's own in its manifest, and a\ndeploy to a host that does not serve one is refused:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">#[berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">program(syscalls \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"berm.get\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"berm.set\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"berm.http.fetch\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> [\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"api.example.com\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">] })]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"who-called\">\u003Ca href=\"#who-called\">Who called\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">match\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">caller\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">()\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">?\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> {\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">    Some\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Caller\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Outside\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(account)) \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">/* someone the host authenticated */\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">    Some\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Caller\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Program\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(name)) \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">/* another program, through berm_lang::call */\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">    None\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">/* the host, for this program's own wake, cron or Stripe event */\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>caller()\u003C/code> is set by the host, never by the caller.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>user()\u003C/code> answers the end user a call runs for, as \u003Ccode>User { issuer, subject }\u003C/code>:\nthe identity provider or program that vouched for them and who they are to\nit. It is carried into every nested call.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>vouch(subject)\u003C/code> has the rest of this invocation, and every call it makes after, run for \u003Ccode>subject\u003C/code>, with the program as the issuer, named as the programs it calls are told it is. The manifest declares \u003Ccode>berm.vouch\u003C/code>, and it is refused in a chain that already runs for a user.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>client()\u003C/code> answers an opaque key naming the outside client for one day, or\n\u003Ccode>None\u003C/code> when the host supplied none. It is carried into every nested call.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>deny(message)\u003C/code> makes an \u003Ccode>Error\u003C/code> that fails the call as refusing its caller.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"state\">\u003Ca href=\"#state\">State\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">let\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> seen \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">get\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"last-run\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">?.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">unwrap_or_default\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">();\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">set\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"last-run\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">&#x26;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">now\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">to_le_bytes\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">())\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">?\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">let\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> config\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">:\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> Config\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">get_json\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"config\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">?.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">unwrap_or_default\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">();\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>get\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>set\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>get_json\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>set_json\u003C/code> read and write the program's own\nkeys. Another program's keys cannot be named.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>get\u003C/code> answers \u003Ccode>None\u003C/code> for a key never written.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Writes are committed when the call returns \u003Ccode>Ok\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>set\u003C/code> is refused in a \u003Ccode>#[query]\u003C/code> tool.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"a-database\">\u003Ca href=\"#a-database\">A database\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">#[berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">program(database \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"migrations\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>database\u003C/code> names a directory of \u003Ccode>*.sql\u003C/code> migrations, applied in name order at\ndeploy. A deploy whose migrations do not begin with the ones already applied\nis refused.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>A kit the program \u003Ccode>uses\u003C/code> keeps its tables in the same database, its migrations applied first and checked the same way under the kit's name. See \u003Ca href=\"../manifest/#kits\">Kits\u003C/a>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>berm_lang::rows::&#x3C;T>(statement, params)\u003C/code> runs one statement, \u003Ccode>params\u003C/code> a tuple bound to its \u003Ccode>?\u003C/code>s, and answers its rows, each a tuple of its columns.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>berm_lang::sql(statement, params)\u003C/code> runs one statement, \u003Ccode>params\u003C/code> a JSON array\nbound to its \u003Ccode>?\u003C/code> placeholders, and answers\n\u003Ccode>{\"columns\": [..], \"rows\": [[..]], \"read\": n, \"written\": n}\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Every statement of one invocation runs in one transaction, committed when it\nreturns \u003Ccode>Ok\u003C/code>. Transaction statements are refused, and so is a write under a\n\u003Ccode>#[query]\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Tables named \u003Ccode>_berm_*\u003C/code> are the runtime's.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">let\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> found \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">sql\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"SELECT title FROM items WHERE id = ?\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"[42]\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">?\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"logs\">\u003Ca href=\"#logs\">Logs\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>emit(topics, data)\u003C/code> emits a log under \u003Ccode>topics\u003C/code>, which a reader filters by.\n\u003Ccode>emit!\u003C/code> emits an \u003Ca href=\"../writing-a-program/#events\">\u003Ccode>#[event]\u003C/code>\u003C/a> struct under its\nname.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>A log is kept beside the call it was emitted in, whatever that call ended as.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>emit\u003C/code> is refused in a \u003Ccode>#[query]\u003C/code> tool.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>trace(message)\u003C/code> writes a line to the host's own trace, not to the program's\nlogs.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"http\">\u003Ca href=\"#http\">HTTP\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">let\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> page \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">http\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">fetch\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">    \"GET\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">    \"https://api.example.com/items\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    &#x26;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">[(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Authorization\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Bearer {secret:example}\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)],\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">    b\"\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">?\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>http::fetch\u003C/code> sends one request and answers \u003Ccode>Response { status, headers, body }\u003C/code>.\nA \u003Ccode>4xx\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>5xx\u003C/code> from the far end is a \u003Ccode>Response\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>It reaches only the hosts the manifest declares under \u003Ccode>berm.http.fetch\u003C/code>, by name or by \u003Ccode>*.domain\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>*\u003C/code> (\u003Ca href=\"../manifest/\">manifest\u003C/a>).\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>http::proxy\u003C/code> sends the same request through the host's proxy, to the hosts\nlisted under \u003Ccode>berm.http.proxy\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>http::fetch_within\u003C/code> sends one request given up when nothing answered within its milliseconds, or at the call's deadline when that comes first; otherwise a request waits for the call's deadline.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>http::fetch_all\u003C/code> sends a batch of \u003Ccode>http::Request\u003C/code>s at once, each to a host declared under \u003Ccode>berm.http.fetch\u003C/code> with its own timeout and the most bytes of its answer's body it takes, and answers each in its place, a refusal or failure answering its own.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>A header value or the body may carry \u003Ccode>{secret:NAME}\u003C/code> for a secret the manifest lists in \u003Ccode>secrets\u003C/code>. The host substitutes it, and the program never holds the value.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>CallError::Refused\u003C/code> means nothing was sent: a host or secret the manifest\ndoes not list, or a secret the host has not granted.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"other-programs\">\u003Ca href=\"#other-programs\">Other programs\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">let\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> top \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">call\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"hn\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"top\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">r#\"{\"limit\": 10}\"#\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">?\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>call(program, tool, args)\u003C/code> calls a \u003Ccode>#[public]\u003C/code> tool of the program itself or\nof one the manifest lists in \u003Ccode>programs\u003C/code>, and answers its result as JSON text.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>CallError::Refused\u003C/code> means nothing ran: a name nothing answers to, or one the\nmanifest does not list. \u003Ccode>CallError::Failed\u003C/code> means the target ran and failed.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>The chain nests at most as deep as the host allows, 4 by default.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"../writing-a-program/#calling-another-program\">Calling another program\u003C/a>\ncovers the typed calls \u003Ccode>declare_program!\u003C/code> generates.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"wakes\">\u003Ca href=\"#wakes\">Wakes\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">after\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">300_000\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"weather\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"poll\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"{}\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">?\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>after(delay, program, tool, args)\u003C/code> has the tool run in \u003Ccode>delay\u003C/code> milliseconds.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>A program holds one wake. Arming another drops the one pending.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>The woken call runs with no caller and carries nothing from the call that\narmed it; what it needs goes in state.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>A \u003Ccode>#[query]\u003C/code> tool cannot arm one.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"the-clock-and-randomness\">\u003Ca href=\"#the-clock-and-randomness\">The clock and randomness\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>now()\u003C/code> answers the host's time, in milliseconds since the Unix epoch.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>random(&#x26;mut buffer)\u003C/code> fills \u003Ccode>buffer\u003C/code> from the host's secure random source. Neither needs declaring.\u003C/p>",{"title":32,"slug":33},"Writing a Program","berm/writing-a-program",{"title":35,"slug":36},"The Manifest","berm/manifest"],"uses":{"params":["slug"]}}]}
